WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.710
Hey, lady.

9
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.070
Hey, lady.

10
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:26.830
How are you?

11
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:28.350
I'm good.

12
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.330
I'm taking an Instagram video.

13
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.150
What?

14
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.250
They can't hear you, though, on my video.

15
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.890
I can hear you in my headphones.

16
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.150
I was doing all these little dance moves.

17
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.310
Oh, I missed that.

18
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:43.290
Right before we record, Sam plays a little bit of Creed's song, our music.

19
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.430
And Jenna and I kind of just bop around and it kind of just helps us get into the episode.

20
00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.690
Every week, we dance to Creed's song.

21
00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.410
Love it.

22
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.450
Well, what are we talking about this week, Angela?

23
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:58.210
Oh, Jenna, I am so excited because we are talking about Phyllis's wedding.

24
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.190
I love it so much.

25
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.130
It's so good.

26
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:07.170
This is season three, episode 15, written by Carolyn Williams and directed by Ken Whittingham.

27
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.030
Summary.

28
00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:08.550
Do it.

29
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:12.750
Phyllis and Bob Vance of Vance Refrigeration are getting married.

30
00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.090
Today is the day.

31
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.890
Phyllis has asked Michael to push her father's wheelchair down the aisle.

32
00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:26.490
But after getting upstaged when Phyllis's dad decides to walk down the aisle, Michael tries

33
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.070
to steal the show and is eventually bounced from the reception by Dwight.

34
00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:37.250
In the meantime, Pam is sad and upset by Jim and Karen's relationship and the fact that

35
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:42.690
Phyllis stole all of her wedding ideas and she leaves the reception with Roy.

36
00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.970
I forgot that Pam left with Roy.

37
00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.150
I forgot.

38
00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:48.310
Me too.

39
00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.350
And I'm Pam.

40
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.790
It's so good, though.

41
00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.870
It's so good.

42
00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.250
But doesn't that happen?

43
00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:58.590
Like if you've been with someone a really long time and then you break up, you get back

44
00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.110
together a couple times before you really break up, right?

45
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:01.770
That's real.

46
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:07.990
Especially you're at a wedding and there's all these couples and the person you want to

47
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.510
be with doesn't seem like they want to be with you.

48
00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.350
All of a sudden, the thing that you know is sitting right next to you.

49
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.230
So you're like, well, OK, I feel like having some loving.

50
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.850
Yeah, I guess so.

51
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:21.650
All right.

52
00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.950
Well, listen, fast fact number one.

53
00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:31.750
A lot of people wrote in Sovereign Hurley, Ellie Trevelyan, Winter Pulver, Leah Barbosa,

54
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.990
Tia Minoski and many more want to know where was the wedding filmed.

55
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:45.630
But then Colby Linderman, Dana Hill, Christina, Carolyn and Jennifer all wanted to know, is

56
00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.690
it the same church where Jim and Pam had their wedding because they look very similar?

57
00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.670
It is not the same church.

58
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.390
It's not the same church.

59
00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:58.650
But listen, before I tell you where Phyllis's wedding was filmed, we got even more mail about

60
00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:58.870
it.

61
00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.510
OK, Charis wrote in to say.

62
00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.650
At some point, Phyllis and Pam both say they are Presbyterians.

63
00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.190
Was the wedding filmed at an actual Presbyterian church?

64
00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:14.210
I'm guessing the answer is yes, because the crew pays a lot of attention to detail and

65
00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.750
Presbyterian churches love maroon carpet.

66
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:24.490
Chris Furr said, I am a pastor in the Christian church Disciples of Christ, a small Protestant

67
00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:28.510
denomination, less than a million people, mostly in the U.S.

68
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.070
and Canada.

69
00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:36.370
In this episode, the Disciples logo is clearly visible around the 20 minute, 32 second mark

70
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.050
as Phyllis and Bob are cutting their wedding cake.

71
00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:44.250
I was curious about the choice to leave that specific banner in the background from a prop

72
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.010
point of view.

73
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.650
It's lighted and it's pretty distinctive.

74
00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:54.970
So he goes on to say, the funny thing about it is that theologically, this would be a perfect

75
00:03:54.970 --> 00:04:00.450
compromise choice for a Lutheran and a Unitarian who like to keep things, quote unquote, spicy.

76
00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.550
Any background on this would be cool, as it is a big hit with our little disciples family.

77
00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:12.850
Yes, we filmed Phyllis's wedding at the First Christian Church of North Hollywood, which is

78
00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:17.350
located in Studio City, and they are a Disciples of Christ Church.

79
00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:18.690
Yes.

80
00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:25.130
So when I first moved to L.A., I was looking for somewhere to go for Easter services, and

81
00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:29.250
I was driving around and I drove past this church and it's such a beautiful church.

82
00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.090
You know, it's the red brick and it has a steep.

83
00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.150
It looks very much like that is what a church looks like.

84
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:34.890
You know what I mean?

85
00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:35.210
Yeah.

86
00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.750
And I drove past it and they had a big sign about their Easter service.

87
00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.190
And I thought, oh, well, I'll go there for Easter services.

88
00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:43.690
And I did.

89
00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.530
And it was very nice.

90
00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.310
Well, I'll give you another little fun fact about this church, Ange.

91
00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:48.830
What?

92
00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.650
This is where Kent Zabornak and his wife, Shelly, got married.

93
00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.030
Oh, come on.

94
00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.370
And guess what?

95
00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:59.470
They just celebrated their 30th wedding anniversary this past May.

96
00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.150
Oh, that's so great.

97
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.170
That's so lovely.

98
00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.390
Congratulations, you guys.

99
00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:10.250
And then, guys, the reception took place in their social hall, which was on the second

100
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:10.650
floor.

101
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:14.830
So we were able to film everything at this one church.

102
00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:15.850
Yes.

103
00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.130
They have a fellowship hall.

104
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.750
And they had, you know, they had the rooms like where Phyllis gets ready.

105
00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:21.230
Yeah.

106
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.630
You know, all of that was already at this church.

107
00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:30.770
Well, incidentally, years later, we filmed a school recital scene for my TV show splitting

108
00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.250
up together in that sort of hall.

109
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:38.930
And our holding room for hair and makeup was that same room where Phyllis is getting ready

110
00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:39.850
before her wedding.

111
00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.470
And there's that famous scene with Michael.

112
00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.190
Yeah.

113
00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.070
And I was like texting everybody.

114
00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.870
I was like blowing up everyone's texts.

115
00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.770
I'm like, I'm in the room where the fart happened.

116
00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.010
Here's another little thing about that church.

117
00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:55.850
I filmed there one day by myself because it's where Philip went to daycare.

118
00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.850
Oh, well, are you ready for fast fact number two?

119
00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:00.830
I am.

120
00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.270
We reached out to Phyllis.

121
00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.950
It's Phyllis's wedding.

122
00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:04.970
I know.

123
00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.510
How could we not talk to Phyllis, you guys?

124
00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.030
We are so thrilled.

125
00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.230
So Phyllis is back in St. Louis.

126
00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:16.770
She moved back there semi-permanently a couple of years ago.

127
00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.130
And she sent in some audio clips.

128
00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:23.950
So the first thing we asked Phyllis was just what was it like to get this script and wear

129
00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.670
a wedding gown?

130
00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:25.970
Here's the fun thing.

131
00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:30.570
Jenna, Phyllis, and I are the three cast members that had big weddings.

132
00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.510
And it's kind of like it is your wedding because it's all about you.

133
00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:35.830
It's kind of really fun.

134
00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:36.850
Yes.

135
00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:37.930
All right.

136
00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.890
So Sam, play her clip.

137
00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:40.830
Hi, ladies.

138
00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:47.950
It's Phyllis Smith, or soon to be known as Phyllis Lappin Vance of Vance Refrigeration,

139
00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.870
at least after this episode, right?

140
00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.170
I was so thrilled when I saw the script.

141
00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:55.550
Let's be truthful.

142
00:06:55.730 --> 00:07:00.070
Every time we had a table read, we'd all get to the table, look at the script.

143
00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.150
And see how many lines we had.

144
00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:09.410
So I was really excited and taken back when I saw that I was getting married to my love

145
00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.270
of my life.

146
00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.970
The whole episode, I really enjoyed it all.

147
00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.530
You ask about my dresses.

148
00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:23.150
Well, back in those days, sounds like the dark ages, but it was early 2000, plus-size women

149
00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.570
didn't have a lot of choices.

150
00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:28.410
We either looked like the grandmother or the great-grandmother or the bride.

151
00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:35.030
There were not a lot of choices to be made for heavyset brides.

152
00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:42.210
And so I was just glad that I had a dress that looked pretty and was pretty comfortable.

153
00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.510
I have to give a shout-out to Wardrobe.

154
00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:47.550
They really, really took care of me.

155
00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:52.670
Every time I had to go to the restroom or anything, you know, they were right there to help me out

156
00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:53.410
with everything.

157
00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.270
But yeah, back in those days, I didn't have a lot of choices.

158
00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.650
And so I just wanted to make sure that my arms were covered.

159
00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:07.170
I have a thing about my arms showing on camera and in public.

160
00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.190
As far as the dress was concerned, yeah, I was happy with it.

161
00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.370
It was fairly comfortable.

162
00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.490
And like I said, Wardrobe really kept me.

163
00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:19.090
They were right there every second of the moment.

164
00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:22.390
Aw, I thought she looked gorgeous in this episode.

165
00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.810
She looked so beautiful.

166
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:28.310
That is the first time I've heard Phyllis's voice in a while.

167
00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:34.550
And Jenna, it just, it really made me tear up when I listened to it the first time when

168
00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.410
she sent them over.

169
00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:36.110
Yeah.

170
00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:41.270
She just, you can just hear Phyllis's just pure, she's just a pure soul.

171
00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.170
You know what I mean?

172
00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:43.970
And you just hear it when she talks.

173
00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:48.310
Do you know what one of my favorite parts of that audio clip was, Ange, was that she

174
00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:53.190
referred to herself as Phyllis Lapp and Vance of Vance Refrigeration.

175
00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:53.690
I know.

176
00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.310
She added it to the end.

177
00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:56.250
I know.

178
00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.130
I love it.

179
00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:00.150
Well, that was so fun to hear, Phyllis.

180
00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:02.590
And she sent in several audio clips, you guys.

181
00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.370
So we're going to hear from her throughout this episode.

182
00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.430
Oh, and she sent in some good stuff.

183
00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:06.970
Yeah.

184
00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:11.730
Fast fact number three is Ken Whittingham, the director of this episode.

185
00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.390
Joined us for an interview.

186
00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:17.130
Ken directed several episodes of The Office, and we just loved him.

187
00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.710
The cast loved Ken.

188
00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.770
And Sam plays interview.

189
00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.880
Ken Whittingham, thank you so much for stopping by.

190
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.200
Hi, Ken.

191
00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:30.480
Hey, hey.

192
00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.520
Thank you for having me.

193
00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.580
It is so nice to see you.

194
00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:34.540
Just so lovely.

195
00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.260
I think about all the great times we had on the show.

196
00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.780
And I haven't seen you guys in so long.

197
00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:42.300
And it's so, so amazing to see your faces.

198
00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.440
We look just the same, right, Ken?

199
00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:45.560
Exactly the same.

200
00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.000
Maybe a little, well, maybe a little younger.

201
00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.420
Oh, okay.

202
00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.160
That's what I would have said as well.

203
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:51.960
Yes.

204
00:09:54.660 --> 00:10:00.080
Well, Ken, we always like to start by asking our guests a little bit about how they got

205
00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.380
their job on The Office.

206
00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:05.120
Can you tell us how you met Greg and how you came to be a part of the show?

207
00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:05.780
Sure.

208
00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:12.220
I got a call from my agent, and he said they're going to redo The Office in America.

209
00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.680
NBC is going to do The Office.

210
00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:16.920
And I was already a big fan of the British version.

211
00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:18.880
I said, sure, I'll go for the interview.

212
00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:24.520
And so they sent me, they actually sent me the DVD, and I didn't have a lot of hope for it.

213
00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.360
I said, oh, man, I hope they don't mess this up because it was such a brilliant show.

214
00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.180
And I watched it, and I was like, wow, this is really good.

215
00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:38.880
So I went in for the interview, and I met with Terry Weinberg and Greg Daniels, and we talked

216
00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:39.320
about it.

217
00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:42.680
And we talked about if America was ready for this type of show.

218
00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:49.160
And we really talked extensively about it, you know, if America was going to get it.

219
00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:56.700
And I was very optimistic in saying that I think America's ready for something different,

220
00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:57.460
something new.

221
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.100
And that's how we met.

222
00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:03.140
We met, I guess it was right before the season started.

223
00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:03.440
Yeah.

224
00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.060
So they had done the pilot.

225
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.640
And then they were looking for directors for the series.

226
00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:09.260
Correct.

227
00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:09.820
Correct.

228
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:10.340
Wow.

229
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:10.780
Yeah.

230
00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:16.360
I can definitely see Greg eating up that conversation, you know, sort of like talking about the show

231
00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:19.900
and how it's going to hit America and how America is going to react to it.

232
00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.160
Like, that's all sort of like, he's so open to those kind of conversations, you know?

233
00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:24.760
Yeah.

234
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.040
We talked a long time about it.

235
00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:28.720
That's basically all we talked about.

236
00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:33.220
Because I referenced, I remember referencing another show that really didn't work that

237
00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.020
well in America.

238
00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:35.960
I think it was called Absolutely Fabulous.

239
00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:37.260
Oh, yeah.

240
00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.380
They tried it in America.

241
00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:44.080
And it was funny because I was going down this road that I really didn't want to go.

242
00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.440
I said, yeah, just like the show, Absolutely Fabulous.

243
00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:49.240
They said, oh, before you say too much, we did that show also.

244
00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.520
We produced this show also.

245
00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.520
It wasn't Greg, it was Jerry Weinberg.

246
00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.400
So they said, well, what did you like about that show?

247
00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:02.240
I said, well, I said, I think everybody, which was true, I think everybody looked too

248
00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:02.700
pretty.

249
00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.340
Everybody was just really good looking.

250
00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.880
And it just didn't feel real, you know?

251
00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.680
Ken, you directed a lot of episodes on The Office and two were on location.

252
00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:16.020
You had Michael's birthday that was at the ice skating rink and now Phyllis' wedding.

253
00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.280
What was it like having us travel and be on location?

254
00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:20.300
It was great.

255
00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:25.020
It was great being outside because sometimes the office can get a little claustrophobic

256
00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.020
and it's very safe.

257
00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:32.740
You know, the challenge to moving outside and going on location is still give it that

258
00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:38.100
feel of Scranton, you know, or someplace other than Studio City.

259
00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:43.720
So, you know, so we didn't want to see palm trees and that.

260
00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.060
So that was a real challenge.

261
00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:50.940
And so during prep, we really prepped heavily to make sure that it looked somewhat like

262
00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.320
Scranton or somewhere else, some place nondescript.

263
00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.220
So that was fun.

264
00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:02.120
And it was just fun to be in new spaces and try different things and kind of open the show

265
00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:02.280
up.

266
00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:07.260
I'm always a big fan of any show that I do going outside and getting into the world a little

267
00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:07.460
bit.

268
00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:11.900
I think something people don't realize is the prep process for an episode.

269
00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.280
How long would you get to prep an episode?

270
00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:16.200
Because we've said we shoot for a week.

271
00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:18.520
But how long was your prep before shooting?

272
00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.120
Our prep was, I believe that show was four days.

273
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:23.920
I believe it was four days.

274
00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:26.380
That's not a lot to move a whole show.

275
00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:27.140
No.

276
00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:27.780
Cow.

277
00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:33.880
And then don't you like ride around in a little van and look at locations like a bunch of you

278
00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:34.940
all crammed in a van?

279
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:35.540
I do.

280
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.580
I have such a memory of you guys loading up and leaving set.

281
00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.860
And we're like, where did they go?

282
00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.640
Yeah, it would really be the first day because they would, they would do it.

283
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.760
They would lock down a couple of like the locations department would lock down a couple

284
00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.400
of options that we would have.

285
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.440
And then I would go to those options, the director and producers.

286
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.540
We would go to those locations.

287
00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:57.720
There might be two or three different places.

288
00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.640
And then we would make the decision then.

289
00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:05.600
And it was all about whether or not it was shootable, you know, just backgrounds and just

290
00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.140
accessibility to the location.

291
00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:08.920
Could we get it?

292
00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:11.940
Could we load cameras in easily and load out easily?

293
00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:16.500
So there are a lot of things we had to, we had to be aware of or be conscious of.

294
00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:20.280
So, yeah, that would be basically on that, on that prep day, that'd be the first thing

295
00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:24.540
we would do is go out and try to lock down the locations because it would take a few days

296
00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.280
to get a permit to use specific locations.

297
00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:33.440
Now, did you have a preference of shooting the episodes inside the office bullpen or outside?

298
00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.120
I didn't really have a preference.

299
00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:40.200
I didn't really have a preference because, you know, the writing was just so good.

300
00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:45.760
It was just, I mean, literally, I was reading Phyllis's wedding yesterday, reading the script

301
00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.060
again.

302
00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:51.200
And it was just so, I don't know, it's just written so well.

303
00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:53.320
I mean, it's just written so well.

304
00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:59.140
So it was just like wherever it was, it didn't matter because the words really kind of drove

305
00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.160
the comedy, you know.

306
00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:05.360
So it was, that's what was great about it, you know.

307
00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:05.660
So.

308
00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:10.380
There were all of these great little moments in this episode, you know, you had the, the

309
00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.600
Pam and Roy dancing and then you had Angela and Dwight outside and then all these little

310
00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.360
vignettes like Michael's head bobbing up in the window.

311
00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:21.380
And what was that like to sort of figure out where those little moments would happen and

312
00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.400
how you captured them?

313
00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.200
Well, what I would do is I kind of, I'm a super prepper.

314
00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:30.440
So I would, I would, I would, I kind of, I think for this episode, I've made a shot list

315
00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.800
and, and the order in which we would go on and go in.

316
00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:39.060
And so what I would do is I kind of hopscotch, I would set up something somewhere else and

317
00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.940
then take a camera and go shoot something else.

318
00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:45.520
And so I was always staying ahead a little bit to be able to capture all that stuff because

319
00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:50.040
that, that episode we had, I was just looking at it a few days ago.

320
00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:55.520
There were so many moments that weren't in the episode that we shot, you know.

321
00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:02.960
And so, and I think typically we would be about six, seven, eight minutes over typically on

322
00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.600
every episode.

323
00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:07.340
So we would shoot more than a lot than we, more than we really needed.

324
00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:13.240
But I would just stay ahead and just try to get it all in, you know, and just, and it

325
00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.100
was very, very planned.

326
00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:19.500
And, and some things, you know, on the day we would, we would do things that weren't planned.

327
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:25.840
Like when Uncle Al went outside, I think initially he was supposed to be sitting on a bench and

328
00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.800
we got outside and it was nighttime.

329
00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:31.920
I said, if he walked into the street, he was green and then he went the opposite way against

330
00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:36.760
traffic and cars came down and literally cars were honking and everything.

331
00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:38.280
So we used all that stuff.

332
00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:38.880
It was written.

333
00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.240
So none of that was scripted.

334
00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:44.620
We just kind of came up with that, you know, off the, off the top of our heads, you know.

335
00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:45.160
So.

336
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.500
That created so much more tension.

337
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.240
Yes.

338
00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.220
Than him just sitting on a bench.

339
00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:50.520
Yes.

340
00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.680
That was such a good idea.

341
00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:55.440
You were really worried he was just going to be wandering off somewhere in the night.

342
00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:56.220
Right.

343
00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:56.720
Exactly.

344
00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.200
Yeah.

345
00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:59.320
I think in the episode, you see the light turn.

346
00:16:59.580 --> 00:16:59.740
Yeah.

347
00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:01.820
So we timed it and everything.

348
00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.260
So there was, that was really a lot of fun.

349
00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.880
I'm glad that made it into the cut.

350
00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:06.760
Yeah.

351
00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:12.360
Well, Ken, I got so tickled just watching that moment when Angela Martin arrives and sees

352
00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:15.960
Dwight and they have that brief exchange, but that, that was kind of it.

353
00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.860
And then, then we had to go into the church.

354
00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:23.160
And I remember playing with you about how do we then like, if you're like, break left,

355
00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:25.880
don't linger, left, and all of that kind of stuff.

356
00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:26.540
Right.

357
00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.740
And I just remember you letting us play a little bit with that.

358
00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.860
And it was so absurd and ridiculous.

359
00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:32.500
Right.

360
00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.180
We just had so much fun.

361
00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.360
That was fun.

362
00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:36.140
That was a lot of fun.

363
00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:40.380
Because I just, I really wanted to create the awkwardness between the two of you, you

364
00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.220
know, because I knew that you were supposed to be meeting Dennis later on.

365
00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:44.040
Yes.

366
00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:48.940
And then, so there had to be this little, you know, this tension, especially when he

367
00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.640
gave you that compliment, you know?

368
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:55.660
And so I think that kind of, you know, I don't know, in my mind, that kind of sealed it.

369
00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:58.000
Like you just became more attractive to him.

370
00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.960
And so it was easier for you to, to kind of blow this other guy off.

371
00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.420
Who was so perfect for her.

372
00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.820
That's a runner, you guys, that didn't make it in the episode.

373
00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:09.460
Phyllis sits Angela next to this guy named Dennis.

374
00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:12.940
She kind of tries to set her up at the, you know, at the reception.

375
00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.140
And Dennis is a vet.

376
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.980
He loves cats and Jesus.

377
00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:23.320
I mean, she chooses Dwight because he told her she looks like the Queen of England.

378
00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:24.540
Exactly.

379
00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:26.400
So funny.

380
00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:27.360
I know.

381
00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:27.880
So, yeah.

382
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.000
I wish, I wish some of the stuff would have made it in, the stuff from Dennis.

383
00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:35.080
But I guess we, again, we just didn't have time.

384
00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.860
But there's so much good stuff in here, you know?

385
00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:38.800
Yeah, yeah.

386
00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:42.840
And we even had, I think it was, I don't think it made it into the episode as well.

387
00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.000
We had Mike going.

388
00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:48.280
There was a chair that kind of, you know those chairs where people can't walk upstairs.

389
00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:48.720
Yes.

390
00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.400
That was going up and down.

391
00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.800
We didn't use any of that either.

392
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.760
We were just, it was just so much.

393
00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:59.420
And that's the beauty about being on location is that you have these spaces that, and you

394
00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.860
get these ideas that you can just do stuff that's not scripted at all.

395
00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:07.240
You know, so that's, that's, that's one of the great things about being on location.

396
00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.460
Well, there are a lot of really great deleted scenes.

397
00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:15.180
So for people that have the DVDs, you have to go see all the other stuff that Ken shot.

398
00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:21.980
People always want to know if the directors of episodes also have to shoot the flashback

399
00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:22.420
moments.

400
00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:27.420
Did you have to shoot that moment with little Michael at his mom's wedding to Jeff?

401
00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:27.840
Yeah.

402
00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:27.940
Yeah.

403
00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:28.900
That was a lot of fun.

404
00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:32.920
That, that was a lot of fun because we, we knew that it needed to look a little vintage

405
00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:39.420
and, and, and so, and we kind of moved the camera like it was old VHS camera, you know,

406
00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:45.480
and, and then we, of course, in, in post, we kind of doctored it, but, but it was really

407
00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:45.820
fun.

408
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:50.560
It was, it was a lot of fun that we, and we, we shot it and we just hoped that it would

409
00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:53.940
look great and look, look vintage, you know, look older.

410
00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:56.180
So I think, I think we achieved it.

411
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:57.320
It looked fantastic.

412
00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:01.140
Do you do that on the first day so that then Michael can watch it later?

