00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:05.260
Yes, we did.

415
00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.800
We shot it on the first day and then we, we played it back.

416
00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:08.980
I believe that's how we did it.

417
00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:13.220
Well, there were so many just fantastic, big setups for this episode.

418
00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:18.740
Was there any moment that was the most challenging to shoot or like something really funny for you?

419
00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:22.120
Just, just one of these scenes that, that just hit you.

420
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:26.240
I don't, I don't think that there was really anything too challenging.

421
00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.400
One, one, there was one scene that was really hard to get through.

422
00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:34.000
And I would say that was kind of challenging because we were just, we could not stop laughing.

423
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:39.020
And that's when, when Michael went into the check on Phyllis to see how she was doing.

424
00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:45.820
And then, and then he said, you know, did you, did you, did you pass gas or break wind?

425
00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:46.100
Did you break wind?

426
00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:47.100
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

427
00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:56.080
And, and, and, you know, the funny thing about that is, um, that was a joke that was put into the script that wasn't really supposed to stay in the script.

428
00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:04.120
That, that was, yeah, that was never really supposed to, it was just like a joke that wouldn't it be funny if this happened?

429
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:12.740
And then it just lived and then, and then it just, I guess Carolyn, Carolyn was telling me, Carolyn Williams, the writer of the episode.

430
00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:21.140
Um, so it just kind of stayed and we just shot it and Michael, you know, Steve was so good.

431
00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:25.700
He could not stop laughing and, and he could not stop laughing.

432
00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.360
I've never seen him break like that.

433
00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:32.000
And we all were just like, it took us about an hour to get through because we could not stop laughing.

434
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:38.140
Well, you know, Phyllis always was able to have such this earnest expression, you know,

435
00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:45.840
and whenever you had to be mean to her or just like have some random line towards her and she would look at you with these sweet eyes.

436
00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:51.600
So I can, I can see Steve not being able to get through it, being like, that is really pungent.

437
00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:53.240
She's just like, hmm.

438
00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:55.780
Right.

439
00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.520
And then he started messing around with her hair and everything.

440
00:21:58.760 --> 00:21:58.820
Oh my God.

441
00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:01.460
And she's just like, okay, you gotta, okay, you gotta go.

442
00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:07.120
I feel like her whole interior monologue was just six weeks vacation, six weeks vacation.

443
00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:07.680
Right.

444
00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:07.980
Yeah.

445
00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:09.760
Because that's what she was going to get.

446
00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:10.440
Right.

447
00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:10.960
Exactly.

448
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.260
That's how she's going to get through it.

449
00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:13.660
Yeah.

450
00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:13.980
Yeah.

451
00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:15.480
With Bob Vance.

452
00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:16.280
Yeah, exactly.

453
00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:18.520
And I loved, I loved in the wedding.

454
00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:23.460
I loved so much that they were like, do you Phyllis take Bob Vance of Vance Refrigeration?

455
00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:24.420
Yeah.

456
00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:27.740
Like his, you're, you're taking the whole thing.

457
00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.540
That's what was so great about that.

458
00:22:29.540 --> 00:22:35.180
I think it was in the merger when she told, when she told Rashida, you know, you don't

459
00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:39.400
know who Bob Vance is, you know, you got a lot to learn, Missy.

460
00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:45.040
And that was, and that's what was so funny about it because Bob Vance is a big deal in

461
00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:46.500
that town, you know?

462
00:22:46.820 --> 00:22:47.160
Yeah.

463
00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.600
So he was all up, you know, it's all about Bob Vance Refrigeration.

464
00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:52.560
Everybody knew him.

465
00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:56.560
So, well, Phyllis is now the first lady of Vance Refrigeration.

466
00:22:57.440 --> 00:22:59.260
I mean, she's going to play the part.

467
00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:00.380
Right, right.

468
00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:02.620
I'm sure she's going to have to go to, I don't know.

