Oscar and I, Oscar and I played music and danced in my trailer.

1237
00:58:34.490 --> 00:58:36.910
Oh, and John's trailer was Hangout Central.

1238
00:58:37.230 --> 00:58:39.350
The guys were playing Madden football in there.

1239
00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:42.210
And we went, us gals, and hung out in there, too.

1240
00:58:42.610 --> 00:58:45.990
Rain actually attempted to teach me how to play Madden.

1241
00:58:46.410 --> 00:58:48.690
Oh, I was horrible.

1242
00:58:48.770 --> 00:58:50.390
And he was so patient.

1243
00:58:50.790 --> 00:58:53.730
At one point, our second AD was trying to find us all.

1244
00:58:53.850 --> 00:58:58.010
And when it came to John's trailer, it was John, Rain, Jenna, Rashida, and me.

1245
00:58:58.230 --> 00:59:00.490
Us gals took turns hosting lunch.

1246
00:59:01.110 --> 00:59:05.290
Today, I hosted and I realized I spent the morning sprucing up my trailer.

1247
00:59:05.290 --> 00:59:06.370
Isn't that crazy?

1248
00:59:06.650 --> 00:59:10.870
I cleaned it and then I lit a candle like I was at home having people over for dinner.

1249
00:59:11.070 --> 00:59:12.190
Of course you did.

1250
00:59:12.470 --> 00:59:13.570
Oh, my gosh.

1251
00:59:13.570 --> 00:59:15.470
This is so cute.

1252
00:59:15.890 --> 00:59:20.610
I think the thing that's striking me, Angela, is that it's true how little time we spent

1253
00:59:20.610 --> 00:59:24.590
in our trailers when we were back on our Dunder Mifflin set because we would just hang out

1254
00:59:24.590 --> 00:59:26.470
at our desks between scenes.

1255
00:59:26.910 --> 00:59:27.390
Exactly.

1256
00:59:27.390 --> 00:59:30.090
That's why I said we didn't have our office desks.

1257
00:59:30.230 --> 00:59:31.170
So, yeah.

1258
00:59:31.170 --> 00:59:31.250
Yeah.

1259
00:59:31.470 --> 00:59:36.630
And I know a lot of these scenes, Jenna, if we weren't in them, they really wanted us

1260
00:59:36.630 --> 00:59:40.510
to go to our trailer because they didn't want, you know, they didn't want to be looking for

1261
00:59:40.510 --> 00:59:41.610
us all throughout the church.

1262
00:59:41.790 --> 00:59:45.670
So when we weren't in scenes, they wanted us to go to our little base camp area.

1263
00:59:46.450 --> 00:59:50.530
And we didn't do as much background work in this episode as you might think.

1264
00:59:50.690 --> 00:59:52.350
They really crafted these shots.

1265
00:59:52.490 --> 00:59:53.850
And Ken kind of talked about that.

1266
00:59:53.970 --> 00:59:59.470
He had a very specific shot list and he knew exactly what he wanted to see and when he

1267
00:59:59.470 --> 01:00:00.330
wanted to see it.

1268
01:00:00.650 --> 01:00:04.430
So if you weren't a part of that storytelling, you were back in the trailer.

1269
01:00:04.770 --> 01:00:04.950
Yeah.

1270
01:00:05.650 --> 01:00:07.950
Learning how to play Madden football from Rainn Wilson.

1271
01:00:08.070 --> 01:00:08.690
I guess so.

1272
01:00:10.830 --> 01:00:15.330
Now that you bring it up, I have a vague memory of Rainn very patiently trying to teach you

1273
01:00:15.330 --> 01:00:16.970
all the buttons on that controller.

1274
01:00:17.110 --> 01:00:17.810
I was horrible.

1275
01:00:18.290 --> 01:00:19.710
Back at the reception.

1276
01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:24.270
I guess on the way into the reception, they have a traditional receiving line.

1277
01:00:24.850 --> 01:00:26.110
Everyone walks through.

1278
01:00:26.450 --> 01:00:28.590
You have a nice little moment with Phyllis.

1279
01:00:28.590 --> 01:00:32.090
Yes, I say that her dress is so white, it's almost blinding.

1280
01:00:32.270 --> 01:00:34.090
I think I know what the implication is there.

1281
01:00:34.230 --> 01:00:34.450
Yes.

1282
01:00:34.570 --> 01:00:37.210
But did you notice that I have little lace gloves on?

1283
01:00:37.530 --> 01:00:37.970
No.

1284
01:00:38.250 --> 01:00:38.670
Yes.

1285
01:00:38.790 --> 01:00:43.230
And I had to wear them the whole week and they drove me crazy.

1286
01:00:43.590 --> 01:00:48.010
Well, you know, they would especially drive you crazy today because you cannot wear lace

1287
01:00:48.010 --> 01:00:49.650
gloves and operate a smartphone.

1288
01:00:50.190 --> 01:00:50.750
Oh, right.

1289
01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:52.870
I wouldn't be able to swipe up or do anything.

1290
01:00:53.250 --> 01:00:53.690
No.

1291
01:00:54.070 --> 01:00:55.170
That was my first thought.

1292
01:00:55.250 --> 01:00:56.710
My first thought when you told me that.

1293
01:00:56.710 --> 01:00:58.950
But then my other thought is, were they itchy?

1294
01:00:59.190 --> 01:01:00.750
They were a little too long for my fingers.

1295
01:01:00.750 --> 01:01:02.490
So I had this little like floppy bit.

1296
01:01:02.850 --> 01:01:03.650
And then...

1297
01:01:03.650 --> 01:01:04.330
That's what she said.

1298
01:01:06.030 --> 01:01:11.090
I have a deleted talking head where I show up to the church and it's one of the craziest

1299
01:01:11.090 --> 01:01:11.510
shots.

1300
01:01:11.630 --> 01:01:12.770
I meant to bring it up to Ken.

1301
01:01:12.890 --> 01:01:13.170
Dang it.

1302
01:01:13.510 --> 01:01:16.190
It's like he put the camera on the ground, Jenna.

1303
01:01:16.190 --> 01:01:20.870
And it's shooting up from the asphalt, like under my chin.

1304
01:01:21.170 --> 01:01:22.210
It's not super flattering.

1305
01:01:22.430 --> 01:01:29.010
And I'm looking down and a high above my head is the cross in the steeple of the church.

1306
01:01:29.290 --> 01:01:34.550
It's a very dramatic talking head where I basically say, you know, I like traditional

1307
01:01:34.550 --> 01:01:34.850
weddings.

1308
01:01:35.050 --> 01:01:36.870
So let's see what this one's going to be like.

1309
01:01:36.870 --> 01:01:41.850
And as I'm doing it, I have black gloves on and I'm taking them off slowly.

1310
01:01:42.070 --> 01:01:44.490
And as I do, underneath are my lace gloves.

1311
01:01:48.150 --> 01:01:50.090
I adore that detail.

1312
01:01:50.090 --> 01:01:52.090
That is very funny.

1313
01:01:52.670 --> 01:01:54.850
So people are milling about.

1314
01:01:55.330 --> 01:01:58.070
People are kind of like, you know, checking out the food.

1315
01:01:58.070 --> 01:01:59.470
They're walking around.

1316
01:02:00.310 --> 01:02:08.110
Kelly finds Pam and she is like, oh, my God, you must be so miserable right now.

1317
01:02:09.050 --> 01:02:09.530
Yeah.

1318
01:02:09.710 --> 01:02:11.210
And Pam's like, I don't know.

1319
01:02:11.270 --> 01:02:11.670
I'm fine.

1320
01:02:11.870 --> 01:02:12.290
I'm OK.

1321
01:02:12.550 --> 01:02:17.390
And she's like, well, she would be freaking out and getting drunk and telling someone she's

1322
01:02:17.390 --> 01:02:17.690
pregnant.

1323
01:02:18.790 --> 01:02:21.410
Pam's like, Pam's like, it's a lot of good ideas.

1324
01:02:22.110 --> 01:02:24.110
I feel like Kelly is a frenemy.

1325
01:02:24.430 --> 01:02:26.530
I feel like she's one of those types of gals.

1326
01:02:26.530 --> 01:02:29.570
Like, clearly, Pam is noticing all of this.

1327
01:02:29.690 --> 01:02:33.050
She really doesn't want anyone to then like rub it in her face.

1328
01:02:33.050 --> 01:02:35.230
But she's like, oh, my God, are you so bummed out?

1329
01:02:35.350 --> 01:02:37.990
Because they totally took your wedding and Roy's here and Jim's with someone else.

1330
01:02:38.150 --> 01:02:39.250
I would be miserable.

1331
01:02:40.170 --> 01:02:40.610
Yes.

1332
01:02:40.690 --> 01:02:43.130
But it's all under the guise of like, are you OK?

1333
01:02:43.650 --> 01:02:43.950
Yeah.

1334
01:02:44.450 --> 01:02:45.270
She doesn't care.

1335
01:02:45.550 --> 01:02:46.530
She doesn't care if you're OK.

1336
01:02:47.210 --> 01:02:47.610
No.

1337
01:02:48.150 --> 01:02:48.590
No.

1338
01:02:48.850 --> 01:02:50.170
This is a gossip moment.

1339
01:02:51.150 --> 01:02:53.790
Well, Dwight is determined to find the wedding crashers.

1340
01:02:54.010 --> 01:02:56.250
Dwight finds an elderly guest at the buffet.

1341
01:02:56.690 --> 01:02:58.970
He's like putting a roll in his pocket.

1342
01:02:59.270 --> 01:03:00.230
I respect that move.

1343
01:03:00.710 --> 01:03:02.770
I have put bread in my purse before.

1344
01:03:03.470 --> 01:03:04.490
I've done it, too.

1345
01:03:05.250 --> 01:03:05.690
Yeah.

1346
01:03:06.330 --> 01:03:07.110
Many times.

1347
01:03:07.210 --> 01:03:07.770
Many times.

1348
01:03:07.890 --> 01:03:08.870
I've done it with you.

1349
01:03:09.030 --> 01:03:10.610
I don't like to be without food.

1350
01:03:10.610 --> 01:03:13.450
I want to have a snack on me at all times.

1351
01:03:13.790 --> 01:03:16.630
OK, so Dwight thinks he's a wedding crasher.

1352
01:03:16.870 --> 01:03:19.610
He starts asking him all these questions and the man is confused.

1353
01:03:19.910 --> 01:03:20.830
And Dwight's like, that's it.

1354
01:03:20.910 --> 01:03:22.030
And kicks him out.

1355
01:03:22.310 --> 01:03:23.650
He kicks him out.

1356
01:03:23.650 --> 01:03:27.270
And that's when Michael checks in with Phyllis.

1357
01:03:28.170 --> 01:03:29.610
Who's like, is everything OK?

1358
01:03:30.150 --> 01:03:33.550
He mentions he sent back the chicken because it was undercooked.

1359
01:03:33.710 --> 01:03:35.330
Phyllis is like, it was fish.

1360
01:03:35.550 --> 01:03:36.810
He's like, I'm on it.

1361
01:03:37.330 --> 01:03:39.750
Well, we had a fan question from Ashley Brooks.

1362
01:03:40.090 --> 01:03:46.130
She wanted to know, did either of you have a funny story or a wildcard guest like Michael

1363
01:03:46.130 --> 01:03:47.230
at your weddings?

1364
01:03:48.410 --> 01:03:49.850
You know, I didn't.

1365
01:03:50.150 --> 01:03:53.010
But two people did have sex in the bushes at my wedding.

1366
01:03:53.790 --> 01:03:54.890
I know one of them.

1367
01:03:55.030 --> 01:03:55.650
It wasn't me.

1368
01:03:55.890 --> 01:04:00.010
Well, I know both of them because they were guests at my wedding and they didn't come

1369
01:04:00.010 --> 01:04:00.530
together.

1370
01:04:01.470 --> 01:04:01.910
What?

1371
01:04:02.430 --> 01:04:04.930
Oh, oh, that sounded weird.

1372
01:04:06.830 --> 01:04:08.070
I don't know that much.

1373
01:04:08.150 --> 01:04:12.210
I don't know that many details about their about their rendezvous.

1374
01:04:12.250 --> 01:04:13.910
I was like, Darren Headlights.

1375
01:04:14.050 --> 01:04:14.610
I was like, what?

1376
01:04:15.370 --> 01:04:16.090
Oh, dear.

1377
01:04:16.550 --> 01:04:16.950
No, no, no.

1378
01:04:16.950 --> 01:04:19.590
They didn't arrive to the wedding.

1379
01:04:19.790 --> 01:04:20.450
Wedding together.

1380
01:04:20.450 --> 01:04:22.330
They hooked up at your wedding.

1381
01:04:22.890 --> 01:04:23.370
Yes.

1382
01:04:23.370 --> 01:04:29.750
OK, well, I can tell you at my wedding, we didn't have a random guest, but my husband

1383
01:04:29.750 --> 01:04:32.350
really, really, really wanted to have a signature drink.

1384
01:04:32.590 --> 01:04:34.510
He was like so excited about it.

1385
01:04:34.770 --> 01:04:36.250
I love a signature drink.

1386
01:04:36.290 --> 01:04:37.570
I know he did, too.

1387
01:04:37.650 --> 01:04:40.610
I was like, but he wanted he likes a Moscow mule.

1388
01:04:40.910 --> 01:04:44.690
So he wanted to have the Moscow mule, but he wanted to use is it bourbon?

1389
01:04:44.810 --> 01:04:45.450
I'm going to get this wrong.

1390
01:04:45.570 --> 01:04:47.430
It's actually called a Kentucky mule.

1391
01:04:47.770 --> 01:04:52.970
They make it a little different, but he wanted everyone as their wedding favor to get

1392
01:04:52.970 --> 01:04:54.290
a copper mug.

1393
01:04:55.210 --> 01:04:56.470
Do you remember this, Jenna?

1394
01:04:57.150 --> 01:04:58.610
I love my copper mug.

1395
01:04:58.710 --> 01:05:00.350
OK, you took yours home.

1396
01:05:01.370 --> 01:05:05.670
Yeah, I told Josh, I was like, Josh, people are not going to realize they can take them

1397
01:05:05.670 --> 01:05:05.890
home.

1398
01:05:06.170 --> 01:05:06.770
They're not.

1399
01:05:06.910 --> 01:05:07.870
And he's like, yes, they will.

1400
01:05:07.970 --> 01:05:09.590
We'll say it's the party favor.

1401
01:05:09.790 --> 01:05:11.170
They get to take a copper mug home.

1402
01:05:11.990 --> 01:05:13.790
Engraved on it was like our wedding date.

1403
01:05:14.130 --> 01:05:16.190
I was like, babe, this is really nice.

1404
01:05:16.450 --> 01:05:17.590
People are not going to take them home.

1405
01:05:17.770 --> 01:05:19.530
And we got into a little fight about it.

1406
01:05:19.650 --> 01:05:20.530
It was planning the wedding.

1407
01:05:21.130 --> 01:05:21.570
Guess what?

1408
01:05:22.290 --> 01:05:22.690
What?

1409
01:05:22.690 --> 01:05:24.270
We have 55 copper mugs.

1410
01:05:24.450 --> 01:05:25.110
Oh, no.

1411
01:05:25.630 --> 01:05:26.350
Oh, no.

1412
01:05:27.670 --> 01:05:30.110
Well, Lee and I both took our mugs home.

1413
01:05:30.270 --> 01:05:33.570
I knew that that was your wedding favor.

1414
01:05:33.570 --> 01:05:33.930
We had a sign.

1415
01:05:33.930 --> 01:05:35.270
Probably because you told me.

1416
01:05:35.270 --> 01:05:36.730
And also, we had a sign.

1417
01:05:37.310 --> 01:05:42.410
It had your table where you went to get seated, tied in a ribbon with your name.

1418
01:05:42.490 --> 01:05:45.570
And they said this copper mug is yours to take home.

1419
01:05:45.910 --> 01:05:51.210
Now, to be fair, Angela, if you had been a guest at your own wedding, would you have read

1420
01:05:51.210 --> 01:05:54.150
the sign and taken home your mug?

1421
01:05:54.290 --> 01:05:56.870
Jenna, when it comes to getting free things, I read.

1422
01:05:58.210 --> 01:05:58.650
Okay.

1423
01:05:59.110 --> 01:05:59.770
That's it.

1424
01:05:59.870 --> 01:06:00.970
You know what I wouldn't have read?

1425
01:06:01.170 --> 01:06:02.710
The instructions on where to park.

1426
01:06:03.690 --> 01:06:04.410
That's correct.

1427
01:06:04.410 --> 01:06:08.810
I would have circled around until I figured it out, but I would have known to take the

1428
01:06:08.810 --> 01:06:09.530
copper mug home.

1429
01:06:09.690 --> 01:06:10.230
Fair enough.

1430
01:06:10.570 --> 01:06:10.910
All right.

1431
01:06:11.130 --> 01:06:12.910
Well, now we have some big news.

1432
01:06:13.890 --> 01:06:17.450
Scrantonicity is going to be playing at Phyllis's reception.

1433
01:06:17.450 --> 01:06:18.190
Yeah.

1434
01:06:18.810 --> 01:06:21.910
She hired Kevin's band, Scrantonicity.

1435
01:06:22.250 --> 01:06:23.830
It's their third gig.

1436
01:06:24.470 --> 01:06:28.290
Their previous two gigs were for members of their own band.

1437
01:06:29.410 --> 01:06:36.090
But before they begin playing their set, Kevin asked the crowd, has anyone seen Uncle Al?

1438
01:06:36.410 --> 01:06:40.530
He has dementia, and his family is really worried about him.

1439
01:06:40.950 --> 01:06:41.470
Roxanne!

1440
01:06:41.470 --> 01:06:44.690
And then he immediately launches into Roxanne.

1441
01:06:44.870 --> 01:06:46.790
The timing of that is so perfect.

1442
01:06:46.790 --> 01:06:49.810
Well, Angela, we got a lot of questions about the band.

1443
01:06:49.990 --> 01:06:56.030
Becky, Hadassah, Marie, Sam, and Sarah all wanted to know, was it really Brian Baumgartner

1444
01:06:56.030 --> 01:06:57.070
singing at the wedding?

1445
01:06:57.250 --> 01:06:59.270
And was he really playing the drums?

1446
01:06:59.550 --> 01:07:00.370
Yes and yes.

1447
01:07:00.550 --> 01:07:01.370
Yes and yes.

1448
01:07:01.470 --> 01:07:03.210
And he practiced, you guys.

1449
01:07:03.350 --> 01:07:04.650
He took it really seriously.

1450
01:07:05.170 --> 01:07:08.490
He worked so hard on that, and I thought he did such a great job.

1451
01:07:09.430 --> 01:07:09.910
Yeah.

1452
01:07:10.150 --> 01:07:11.870
Well, I have an observation, Jenna.

1453
01:07:12.550 --> 01:07:15.590
Wasn't this also the band that was going to play at Pam's wedding?

1454
01:07:16.210 --> 01:07:16.690
Yep.

1455
01:07:16.790 --> 01:07:18.670
So put it on the liSt.

1456
01:07:19.290 --> 01:07:20.650
Put it on the liSt.

1457
01:07:20.790 --> 01:07:27.630
And speaking of, Roy is about to find Pam, and he tells her he is so impressed by all

1458
01:07:27.630 --> 01:07:31.210
the details at this wedding and that Phyllis has such great taste.

1459
01:07:31.330 --> 01:07:31.650
Mm-hmm.

1460
01:07:31.810 --> 01:07:33.470
Well, Jenna, there is a deleted scene.

1461
01:07:33.630 --> 01:07:34.390
It's fantastic.

1462
01:07:34.910 --> 01:07:40.530
Phyllis comes up to Pam at the reception and is like, hey, you might have noticed that

1463
01:07:40.530 --> 01:07:46.350
Bob and I use the same after-dinner mints, like, party favor from your wedding that you

1464
01:07:46.350 --> 01:07:46.750
had planned.

1465
01:07:46.750 --> 01:07:47.790
I hope that's okay.

1466
01:07:48.490 --> 01:07:52.070
And you're like, basically, Pam's like, uh, just the mints?

1467
01:07:52.450 --> 01:07:54.030
So wait, can you play it, Sam?

1468
01:07:54.030 --> 01:07:54.890
I recorded it.

1469
01:07:55.290 --> 01:07:56.490
Are you enjoying yourself?

1470
01:07:56.890 --> 01:07:57.470
Oh, yeah.

1471
01:07:57.630 --> 01:07:58.610
I'm having a great time.

1472
01:07:58.990 --> 01:07:59.330
Good.

1473
01:07:59.710 --> 01:08:03.450
You know, I don't know if you noticed, but Bob and I borrowed your idea for the after-dinner

1474
01:08:03.450 --> 01:08:05.050
mints that you were going to have at your wedding.

1475
01:08:05.050 --> 01:08:06.290
Oh, yeah.

1476
01:08:06.690 --> 01:08:09.410
That and also everything.

1477
01:08:11.330 --> 01:08:17.010
I mean, the dress and the flowers and the fish and the cake.

1478
01:08:17.370 --> 01:08:19.250
You really sound like you're keeping track.

1479
01:08:19.970 --> 01:08:20.950
Oh, I juSt...

1480
01:08:20.950 --> 01:08:23.830
You know, I could make an announcement if what you want is credit.

1481
01:08:26.010 --> 01:08:27.050
No, I...

1482
01:08:27.050 --> 01:08:27.850
Okay.

1483
01:08:28.050 --> 01:08:29.770
Well, maybe I should just move along.

1484
01:08:30.790 --> 01:08:32.730
Oh, that is amazing.

1485
01:08:32.770 --> 01:08:34.810
I mean, how passive-aggressive is that?

1486
01:08:35.050 --> 01:08:37.870
Would you like me to make an announcement so you can get credit?

1487
01:08:38.090 --> 01:08:39.510
It's so amazing.

